<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
{#- Sentence catalog: the engine emits signal/flag KINDS plus named counter
    values; every sentence an operator reads lives here. A new report
    language is a copy of this file with translated macro bodies. -#}
{%- macro signal_text(s, kinds=None) -%}
{%- if s.kind.value == 'zero_traffic_errors' -%}
Receive errors advanced {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.delta_input_errors) }} (~{{ s.values.errors_per_second }}/s) while the device-reported input rate was {{ s.values.input_rate_pps if s.values.input_rate_pps != -1 else '?' }} pps{% if s.values.last_input_minutes != -1 %} and last input was {{ window(s.values.last_input_minutes) }} prior{% endif %}. Errors are accumulating without valid traffic, which places the fault at the link, not in the traffic.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'unattributed_rx_dominant' -%}
{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.unattributed_rx) }} of {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.input_errors) }} input errors ({{ '%.1f'|format(100 * s.values.unattributed_rx / s.values.input_errors) }}%) fall in no named bucket, consistent with symbol-level corruption{% if s.values.runts != -1 %}. runts/UnderSize: {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.runts) }}{% endif %}.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'runts_dominant_no_collisions' -%}
Runts dominate the input-error total with zero collision activity: frames are not surviving to the MAC.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'fcs_fraction_active' -%}
FCS errors are {{ '%.1f'|format(100 * s.values.fcs_fraction) }}% of input errors: frames are arriving but corrupted — marginal signal rather than link-level corruption.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'buffer_group_dominant' -%}
{% if s.values.buffer_group is defined %}Overrun/ignored/no-buffer/input-queue drops account for {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.buffer_group) }} of {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.input_errors) }} input errors in the window: congestion or buffer pressure, not a media problem.{% else %}{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.discards) }} {{ s.values.direction }} discards at meaningful rate: frames arrived intact and were dropped — oversubscription, policer, or ring sizing, not media.{% endif %}
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'discards_without_congestion_signature' -%}
{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.discards) }} {{ s.values.direction }} discards at meaningful rate with no buffer-pressure signature beside them (overrun/ignored/no-buffer flat): consistent with policy drops — an unallowed VLAN on the trunk, an ACL, or storm-control — rather than congestion. Check policy before provisioning capacity.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'reliability_degraded' -%}
Interface reliability {{ s.values.reliability }}/255: the device's own error-weighted average reports the link as degraded (255/255 is healthy).
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'late_collisions_full_duplex' -%}
{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.late_collisions) }} late collisions on a {{ s.values.duplex }}-duplex link{% if s.values.neighbor_duplex is defined and s.values.neighbor_duplex not in ('?', '') %} (neighbor {{ s.values.neighbor_name }}{% if s.values.neighbor_platform is defined and s.values.neighbor_platform not in ('?', '') %}, {{ s.values.neighbor_platform }},{% endif %} reports {{ s.values.neighbor_duplex }}){% endif %}: negotiation/duplex mismatch — fixed via CLI, not by touching media.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'giants_with_mtu_mismatch' -%}
Giants dominate the error profile ({{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.giants) }}, local MTU {{ s.values.mtu }}): consistent with an MTU mismatch between ends. The far end's MTU is not known to this tool — unresolved.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'speed_below_capability' -%}
Link negotiated {{ s.values.speed }} on a {{ s.values.media_type }} port{% if kinds and ('unattributed_rx_dominant' in kinds or 'runts_dominant_no_collisions' in kinds or 'zero_traffic_errors' in kinds) %} while symbol-level corruption dominates the receive errors: 1000BaseT needs all four pairs, and a damaged pair forces exactly this fallback — one damaged-pair story explains the speed, the corruption{% if 'interface_resets' in kinds %}, and the resets{% endif %}. Still consistent with a genuinely 100M endpoint — the TDR resolves it{% else %}. Consistent with damaged pairs forcing a fallback, but equally consistent with a genuinely 100M endpoint — unresolved{% endif %}.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'bytes_per_frame_above_mtu' -%}
Byte counter implies ~{{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.bytes_per_frame) }} B/frame against MTU {{ s.values.mtu }}, indicating errored octets are being counted — weak corroboration of PHY-level errors.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'dom_rx_out_of_range' -%}
DOM receive power {{ '%.1f'|format(s.values.dom_rx_power_dbm) }} dBm is outside {{ '%g'|format(s.values.dom_rx_low_dbm) }}..{{ '%g'|format(s.values.dom_rx_high_dbm) }} dBm: degraded optical path.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'fault_onset_estimate' -%}
The lifetime total at the current rate spans {{ window(s.values.onset_minutes) }} — matching the {{ window(s.values.last_input_minutes) }} since the last valid frame. The fault has likely run at this rate since valid traffic stopped: a concrete date to correlate with change windows.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'zero_delta_nonzero_lifetime' -%}
The lifetime counter is large ({{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.values() | first) }}) but did not move between this tool's two observations: an old event, not an incident. Nobody needs to be dispatched.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'low_fcs_does_not_clear_media' -%}
FCS-Err is only {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.fcs_errors) }} of {{ '{:,}'.format(s.values.input_errors) }}. Low FCS does not rule out media faults: symbol corruption and short frames are discarded before the FCS check, so severe link damage can present with near-zero FCS. Verdict retained.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'interface_resets' -%}
{{ s.values.interface_resets }} interface resets{% if s.values.resets_per_year is defined %} (~{{ s.values.resets_per_year }}/year over the counter's life){% endif %}.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'errors_stopped_after_clear' -%}
If the errors stop advancing after a coordinated manual counter clear and a repoll, with the port otherwise untouched, reclassify HISTORIC_NOT_ACTIVE.
{%- elif s.kind.value == 'errors_resumed' -%}
If the counter advances again on a future run, the case reopens and is reclassified.
{%- else -%}
{{ s.kind.value }}: {{ s.values }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{#- Remediation is derived from the observed media type: a copper port is
    never told to check a transceiver, and DOM absence on copper is expected.
    Every action here is performed by a human; the tool never executes any. -#}
{%- macro next_steps(r) -%}
{%- set media = ((r.stats.media_type if r.stats else '') or '') | lower | replace('-', '') -%}
{%- set copper = 'baset' in media -%}
{%- set fiber = r.stats and r.stats.dom_rx_power_dbm is not none -%}
{%- set category = r.verdict.category.value -%}
{%- set bundle_case = r.verdict.member_findings and not r.parent_portchannel -%}
{%- set clear_target = 'the culpable member interface (the bundle aggregates its members)' if bundle_case else 'this interface' -%}
{%- if category == 'PHYSICAL_MEDIA' -%}
{%- if copper -%}
<p class="muted"><strong>Next steps — non-disruptive:</strong> identify the attached device and its native speed; inspect the patch cord and the jack{% if r.stats and r.stats.interface_resets %}; correlate the error history with the interface resets{% endif %}. DOM is not implemented on this copper port — expected, not a finding.</p>
<p class="muted"><strong>Disruptive, coordinate first:</strong> TDR (<code>test cable-diagnostics tdr</code>) on {{ r.case.interface }}; a manual counter clear on {{ clear_target }} and a repoll at 24&nbsp;h to establish a clean baseline.</p>
{%- elif fiber -%}
<p class="muted"><strong>Next steps — non-disruptive:</strong> inspect and clean the fiber connectors and patch panel; check the transceiver's DOM receive-power trend (this reading: {{ '%.1f'|format(r.stats.dom_rx_power_dbm) }} dBm — a single reading, not a trend); verify the optic is seated.</p>
<p class="muted"><strong>Disruptive, coordinate first:</strong> a manual counter clear and a repoll at 24&nbsp;h; replace the transceiver if DOM stays out of range.</p>
{%- else -%}
<p class="muted"><strong>Next steps — non-disruptive:</strong> inspect the physical path.{% if media and not copper %} DOM could not be read from the transceiver output on this port — check it manually.{% endif %}</p>
<p class="muted"><strong>Disruptive, coordinate first:</strong> a manual counter clear on {{ clear_target }} and a repoll at 24&nbsp;h.</p>
{%- endif -%}
{%- elif category == 'LINK_NEGOTIATION' -%}
{%- set phone = r.stats and ('phone' in (r.stats.neighbor_platform or '') | lower or (r.stats.neighbor_name or '').startswith('SEP')) -%}
<p class="muted"><strong>Next steps:</strong> fix via CLI — align speed/duplex (and MTU where giants dominate) on both ends.{% if phone %} The endpoint is a managed IP phone: its speed/duplex is set from the call manager (CUCM), not at the jack.{% endif %} Not a media dispatch.</p>
{%- elif category == 'CONGESTION_BUFFER' -%}
{%- set policy = r.verdict.signals | selectattr('kind.value', 'equalto', 'discards_without_congestion_signature') | list -%}
{% if policy %}<p class="muted"><strong>Next steps:</strong> check the port's policy first — trunk allowed VLANs, ACL hit counters, storm-control — before provisioning capacity; the buffer-side counters are flat. Not a media dispatch.</p>{% else %}<p class="muted"><strong>Next steps:</strong> review oversubscription, policers, and buffer/ring sizing on this path. Not a media dispatch.</p>{% endif %}
{%- elif category == 'HISTORIC_NOT_ACTIVE' -%}
<p class="muted"><strong>Next steps:</strong> coordinate a manual counter clear, then requeue for a future run. Do not dispatch anyone.</p>
{%- endif -%}
{%- if r.stats and r.stats.vpc_status and r.stats.vpc_status | lower == 'up' and category in ('PHYSICAL_MEDIA', 'LINK_NEGOTIATION', 'CONGESTION_BUFFER') %}
<p class="muted">This port serves vPC {{ r.stats.vpc_number }} and the vPC is up: the peer switch carries a leg to the same host, so member-level remediation can be hitless — verify the peer leg is healthy first, and check it for the same errors.</p>
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro dq_text(f) -%}
{%- if f.kind.value == 'stale_poll_timestamp' -%}
CSV poll timestamp is {{ window(f.values.staleness_minutes) }} old at report time; the CSV's rates describe that period, not the present.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'interval_from_ingest_time' -%}
Interval ({{ window(f.values.interval_minutes) }}) derived from host-side timestamps, not device time.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'delta_source_disagreement' -%}
Δ sources disagree: iftriage run-to-run {{ '{:,}'.format(f.values.delta_tool) }} vs CSV change {{ '{:,}'.format(f.values.delta_csv) }}. The tool's own delta is used for rate math (its interval is measured); the CSV export does not state its delta window and it has proven inconsistent across rows — confirm it in the Splunk search before comparing the two figures.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'reconciliation_skew' -%}
Input-error reconciliation is off by {{ f.values.residual }} — consistent with the counters advancing (~{{ f.values.errors_per_second }}/s) between the two show commands, not an accounting problem.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'counter_reconciliation_failed' -%}
Input-error reconciliation does not balance: residual {{ '{:,}'.format(f.values.residual) }} ({{ '%.1f'|format(100 * f.values.residual_fraction) }}% of the total).
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'no_second_observation' -%}
Single observation: no earlier sample could be subtracted, so this report cannot say whether the counter is moving now.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'ratio_out_of_range' -%}
A ratio fell outside 0..100% and was suppressed ({{ f.values.detail }}): its operands come from different populations.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'null_rule_input' -%}
Unknown input(s) to a fired rule: {{ f.values.fields }}. Confidence capped.
{%- elif f.kind.value == 'poll_timezone_assumed_utc' -%}
The CSV `_time` column carries no timezone; UTC was assumed.
{%- else -%}
{{ f.kind.value }}: {{ f.values }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Interface Error Triage — {{ generated_at }}</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif; margin: 2em auto;
         max-width: 900px; color: #1a1a1a; line-height: 1.45; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.4em; } h2 { font-size: 1.15em; margin-top: 1.6em; }
  .summary { background: #f4f6f8; border: 1px solid #d6dbe0; border-radius: 6px;
             padding: 0.9em 1.2em; font-size: 1.05em; }
  .dq { background: #fff8e6; border: 1px solid #e6d9a8; border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 0.7em 1.1em; margin: 0.5em 0; }
  .case { border: 1px solid #d6dbe0; border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.8em 1.2em;
          margin: 0.8em 0; }
  .verdict { font-weight: 700; padding: 0.1em 0.5em; border-radius: 4px;
             display: inline-block; }
  .confidence { font-weight: 600; color: #444; }
  .v-PHYSICAL_MEDIA       { background: #fde3e3; color: #8f1d1d; }
  .v-LINK_NEGOTIATION     { background: #fdefd8; color: #8a5a00; }
  .v-CONGESTION_BUFFER    { background: #e3ecfd; color: #1d3f8f; }
  .v-HISTORIC_NOT_ACTIVE  { background: #eef2e5; color: #4a5c1e; }
  .v-INSUFFICIENT_DATA    { background: #f0ecec; color: #6b4a4a; }
  .v-IGNORE               { background: #e5f5e6; color: #1e6b2a; }
  .v-UNVERIFIED           { background: #ececec; color: #555; }
  .v-PARSE_ERROR          { background: #f3e3fd; color: #5d1d8f; }
  details { margin-top: 0.6em; }
  pre { background: #0f1720; color: #d8e1ea; padding: 0.8em; border-radius: 6px;
        overflow-x: auto; font-size: 0.8em; }
  .muted { color: #667; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .evidence, .against { margin: 0.4em 0 0.4em 0; }
  .against { border-left: 3px solid #c9a; padding-left: 0.8em; }
  table.kv td { padding: 0.05em 0.9em 0.05em 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Interface Error Triage — Top-{{ summary.total }} verification</h1>
<p class="muted">Generated {{ generated_at }} · source: {{ meta.csv_file }}
{% if meta.baseline %} · baseline: {{ meta.baseline.matched }} of {{ meta.baseline.total }} case(s) compared against an earlier stored sample{% endif %}
{% if meta.error_rate_percent %} · thresholds: errors {{ "%g"|format(meta.error_rate_percent) }}% / discards {{ "%g"|format(meta.discard_rate_percent) }}% of frames{% endif %}</p>

{% if meta.from_history %}
<div class="dq"><strong>Rebuilt from stored collection</strong> — no device was
contacted for this report. Device data comes from {{ meta.collected_from }}.</div>
{% endif %}
<div class="summary"><strong>Executive summary:</strong> {{ summary.line }}</div>

{% if findings %}
<h2>Data quality (surfaced, not analyzed)</h2>
{% for f in findings %}
<div class="dq"><strong>{{ f.kind.replace('_', ' ') }}</strong>
{% if f.rows %} (rows {{ f.rows | join(', ') }}){% endif %}<br>
{{ f.detail }}</div>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<h2>Cases</h2>
{% for r in results %}
<div class="case">
  <div>
    <span class="verdict v-{{ r.verdict.category.value if r.verdict else 'UNVERIFIED' }}">
      {{ r.verdict.category.value if r.verdict else 'UNVERIFIED' }}</span>
    {% if r.verdict and r.verdict.confidence %}<span class="confidence">confidence {{ r.verdict.confidence.value }}</span>{% endif %}
    &nbsp;<strong>{{ r.case.switch }}</strong> — {{ r.case.interface }}
    ({{ r.case.counter }})
  </div>
  {% if r.case.description %}<div class="muted">{{ r.case.description }}</div>{% endif %}
  <p>{{ r.verdict.reason if r.verdict else 'No verdict.' }}</p>
  {% if r.verdict and r.verdict.signals %}
  {% set supporting = r.verdict.signals | rejectattr('contradicts') | list %}
  {% set kinds = r.verdict.signals | map(attribute='kind.value') | list %}
  {% set against = r.verdict.signals | selectattr('contradicts') | list %}
  {% if supporting %}
  <div class="evidence"><strong>Evidence</strong>
  <ul>{% for s in supporting %}<li>{{ signal_text(s, kinds) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if against %}
  <div class="against"><strong>Evidence against</strong>
  <ul>{% for s in against %}<li>{{ signal_text(s, kinds) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.verdict and r.verdict.metrics %}
  {% set m = r.verdict.metrics %}
  <table class="kv muted">
    {% if m.delta_tool is not none %}<tr><td>Δ (iftriage, run-to-run)</td><td>{{ '{:,}'.format(m.delta_tool) }}{% if m.interval_minutes %} over {{ window(m.interval_minutes) }} ({{ m.interval_source }}){% endif %}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if m.delta_csv is not none %}<tr><td>Δ (CSV, Splunk window)</td><td>{{ '{:,}'.format(m.delta_csv) }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if m.errors_per_second is not none %}<tr><td>Error rate</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(m.errors_per_second) }}/s ({{ '{:,.0f}'.format(m.errors_per_hour) }}/h)</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if m.error_ratio is not none %}<tr><td>Error ratio</td><td>{{ '%.4f'|format(100 * m.error_ratio) }}% of {{ m.ratio_basis or 'received frames' }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.verdict and r.verdict.data_quality %}
  <p class="muted"><strong>Data quality:</strong></p>
  <ul class="muted">{% for f in r.verdict.data_quality %}<li>{{ dq_text(f) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.verdict and r.verdict.what_would_change %}
  <p class="muted"><strong>What would change this:</strong> {{ signal_text(r.verdict.what_would_change) }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.verdict %}{{ next_steps(r) }}{% endif %}
  {% if r.duplicate_of %}
  <p class="muted">Note: member of {{ r.duplicate_of }}, which is also in this
  report — same underlying issue counted twice.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% set judged_on_counters = r.stats and (not r.verdict or r.verdict.category != VerdictCategory.PARSE_ERROR) %}
  {% if judged_on_counters and r.baseline_taken_at %}
  <p class="muted">Compared against the sample from
  {{ r.baseline_taken_at.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC') }}
  ({{ window(r.baseline_minutes) }} earlier, run #{{ r.baseline_run_id }}).</p>
  {% elif judged_on_counters %}
  <p class="muted">Single-sample verdict: no earlier sample for this
  interface{% if r.baseline_note %} ({{ r.baseline_note }}){% endif %}. This
  report cannot say whether the counter is moving now; run again later for a
  delta.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.verdict and r.verdict.member_findings %}
  <p class="muted">{% if r.parent_portchannel %}Other members of
    {{ r.parent_portchannel }} (context — the verdict above is for
    {{ r.case.interface }} itself):{% else %}Member interfaces:{% endif %}</p>
  <ul class="muted">
    {% for member, finding in r.verdict.member_findings.items() %}
    <li><strong>{{ member }}</strong>: {{ finding }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.recurrence > 1 %}
  <p class="muted">Recurrence: this interface has appeared in {{ r.recurrence }}
  ingested top-20 lists.{% if r.chronic_benign %} Every stored verdict for it is IGNORE — a chronic benign resident: the top-20 ranks by absolute delta, so a busy link's negligible ratio holds a seat permanently, displacing ports with real faults. Consider re-ranking the Splunk search by error ratio, or excluding this interface, rather than re-triaging it.{% endif %}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.case.dq_flags %}
  <p class="muted">Data-quality flags: {{ r.case.dq_flags | join(', ') }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.verdict and r.verdict.details %}
  <p class="muted">{{ r.verdict.details | join(' · ') }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.raw_outputs %}
  <details><summary>Raw evidence ({{ r.raw_outputs | length }} commands)</summary>
    {% for key, raw in r.raw_outputs.items() %}
    <p class="muted">{{ key }}</p>
    <pre>{{ raw }}</pre>
    {% endfor %}
  </details>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}

<p class="muted">iftriage is a read-only diagnostic tool. {% if meta.from_history %}No command was sent: this report was rebuilt from stored data.{% else %}Every command sent is
recorded in the session audit log{% if meta.audit_log %} ({{ meta.audit_log }}){% endif %}.{% endif %}</p>
</body>
</html>
